=== NEARS-3544 task_bug: dart:developer log() diagnostic invisible to logcat/flutter-run console ===

AC2 asks to confirm the NEW debug-mode diagnostic line fires:
  log('AnalyticsService: FirebaseAnalytics.instance unresolvable: $e');  // analytics_service.dart:59
  log('AnalyticsService.$label failed: $e');                            // analytics_service.dart:129

Both use dart:developer's log() (imported line 2: import 'dart:developer';).
This file's OWN doc comment (lines 151-155, on why _mirror uses debugPrint instead)
already documents that dart:developer log() does NOT echo to stdout/logcat -- only to
the VM service Logging stream -- which is exactly the NEARS-262 defect this same file
fixed for the debug mirror. The NEW NEARS-3544 catch blocks re-introduce that same
anti-pattern instead of reusing debugPrint/AppLogger.

Empirical confirmation (this QA run, emulator-5554, suffixed boot, 2194-line full logcat
capture + flutter run's own stdout, both saved as ac2-full-boot-logcat.log /
flutter-run-suffixed2.log):
  grep -F 'AnalyticsService: FirebaseAnalytics.instance unresolvable' -> 0 hits in EITHER channel

Mechanistic proof the catch WAS reached anyway (so this is an observability gap, not a
functional defect -- AC1/AC2's core behaviour is verified independently):
  1. W/FirebaseApp: 'Default FirebaseApp failed to initialize because no default options
     were found' (native layer confirms zero [DEFAULT] app this boot)
  2. logAppOpen()'s _mirror fires (📊 analytics: app_open {}) immediately followed
     synchronously by _safe(), which reads _analytics before any await
  3. Zero E/flutter, zero [core/no-app], zero uncaught FlutterError across the whole
     2194-line capture -> the throw was necessarily caught internally

Impact: Low severity, non-blocking to this ticket's core fix (app does not hang, no
unhandled exception). But the diagnostic added specifically to help a future QA/dev
distinguish 'silently swallowed by design' from 'never reached' is itself unobservable
via the standard QA channel (adb logcat / flutter run stdout), defeating its own purpose.

Suggested fix: swap both log(...) calls (lines 59, 129) to debugPrint(...) or
AppLogger.failure/.warn, matching the file's own NEARS-262 precedent for _mirror.
